==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tesalan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lufalan Pasalan''' at level 30 by using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other Cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Tesalan Pasalan is one of the heaviest-hitting units in the game when it comes to both general enemies and bosses, due in no small part with its extreme range and DPS. In addition to this, it does enough critical damage to immediately destroy any metal enemy in the game, but the low critical chance of 10% is not to be relied on in this aspect, being more of a bonus in general use.

Its impressive offense is balanced with Single Attack, making it pointless if a boss is protected by peon spam or constant support. Be sure to clear the path with long-ranged units, [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave units]] (e.g. [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera Cat]], [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]] etc.) or the default [[Cat Cannon]]. Sometimes even its high range is unable to keep it safe, so think twice about bringing it in stages with LD/Wave/Surge enemies due to its extreme cooldown. Otherwise, on stages with little to no such threats, it will steamroll them when backed properly.

==='''True Form'''===
Lufalan Pasalan can be used on longer ranged enemies that it would previously be unable to reach and on the same enemies more safely; thanks to its increased range, it can also outrange enemies like [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird Cat]], [[Manic Flying Cat (Enemy)|Manic Flying Cat]], [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]], [[Director Kurosawah]] and [[The Perfect Cyclone]].

It also gains a 10% boost in critical chance (for a total chance of 20% per hit), which gives it slightly more consistency against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]] but even then the slow attack rate and low critical hit chance doesn't make it reliable against them, so it merely improves overall DPS. This improvement makes it easier for it to potentially exploit [[Metal Cyclone]]'s very slow movement speed and slightly short range by landing a critical hit and obliterating Metal Cyclone immediately.

==='''Talents'''===
HP Buff, Weaken Immune, and Surge Resist are nearly useless due to Lufalan's terrible survivability and the overly situational nature of the latter two. If you have boosted it with [[Catseye]]s, then the Attack Buff is easily the most useful talent, as it improves this unit's selling point, the already high damage, by up to 20%, resulting in a terrifying value of '''nearly 240,000 per hit at level 50!''' Similarly, Crit Chance Up increases overall DPS too, but by much less; in return, however, it makes Lufalan more consistent in case of Metal Enemies. However, Surge resist can come in handy with a S rank Surge Resist orb, which makes him a very useful nuker against the likes of [[Medu-san]], [[Kappy Jr.]], [[Kappy Kawano]], and other surge enemies, however, the chance of getting a fully maxed surge resist orb is very unlikely, and even A wouldn't be enough for him to survive very long against surge spammers. Nonetheless, Lufalan doesn't have very good talent orb usage besides some of the other ability orbs, so it's still a good orb to use if Surge Resist is maxed out.

